    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Adjunct-Microsoft Office Instructor.html": {
      "title": "Job Title: Adjunct- Microsoft Office Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct-Microsoft Office Instructor-Farmington/Bonne Terre, MO  | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrarâs Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Adjunct-Microsoft Office Instructor-Farmington Bonne Terre MO Area Adjunct-Microsoft Office Instructor-Farmington/Bonne Terre, MO Date Posted: June 17, 2026 Job Title: Adjunct- Microsoft Office Instructor Farmington & Bonne Terre, MO Area (Part-Time) GENERAL SUMMARY : Adjunct Instructor to teach individuals in Missouri correctional facilities located in Farmington and Bonne Terre, Missouri. Individual will be responsible for teaching Introduction to Windows, Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint in a face-to-face and hybrid format.  Teaching assignments will be made in collaboration with the Office of the Provost. This position is a project-oriented instructional position with a goal of outcomes-based objectives and certification in all Microsoft products covered – Microsoft Office User Specialists (MOS). In depth coverage of Word, Excel, and PowerPoint will be covered along with document integration between the various software components and the MOS certification objectives. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Plan and deliver learning experiences for students to make maximum use of class and lab time. Complete assigned teaching load both using Canvas (Lantern) and from inside the correctional facility. Deliver classroom lectures using effective, evidence-based teaching strategies by facilitating student learning through interactive activities, assignments, projects, discussion, and other activities as appropriate for the course. Evaluate student performance. Evaluation of student performance in classroom includes evaluation of assignments and projects, and returning these to students in timely fashion. Identify students requiring academic intervention and refer to appropriate support services Perform other duties as assigned. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor’s degree with Microsoft User Certifications preferred Microsoft User Specialist Certification preferred Teaching experience preferred Experience with Certiport Exam delivery, proctoring, and the certification process preferred. CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\tÂ©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Adjunct-Nursing Faculty.html": {
      "title": "Job Title: Adjunct-Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrarâs Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Adjunct-Nursing Faculty Adjunct Nursing Faculty Date Posted: December 15, 2025 Job Title: Adjunct-Nursing Faculty General Summary : Faculty teach an average of 12 hours of load per academic year. Academic load can be made up of face-to-face courses, hybrid courses, and/or clinical/lab/simulation experiences. Teaching assignments will be made in collaboration with the Nursing Program Director and the Dean of the School of Health Professions. Primary Duties & Responsibilities : Plan and deliver learning experiences for nursing students to make maximum use of class/lab/clinical time. Complete assigned nursing education load. Deliver assigned didactic (classroom) lectures using effective, evidence-based teaching strategies by facilitating student learning through interactive activities, case studies, discussion, and other activities as appropriate for the course. Evaluate student performance. Evaluation of student performance in classroom includes evaluation of papers, projects, and journals, etc. and returning these to students in timely fashion. Attend department meetings and participate in committees as assigned. Hold office hours or provide scheduled availability for student questions, or clarification of course content. Identify students requiring academic intervention and refer to appropriate support services Uphold all institutional, state board of nursing, and accreditation requirements, including the Missouri State Board of Nursing Minimum Standards Perform other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Qualifications For undergraduate pre-licensure programs: MSN preferred Teaching experience preferred RN, MSN-in-Process within one year of graduation mandatory. Current, unencumbered, Missouri nursing license. Approval by the Missouri State Board of Nursing as a faculty member. Physical Requirements For face-to-face courses: Frequently stand for at least one hour consecutively. Operate classroom audio-visual equipment. Speak loudly and clearly enough to be understood by students. Other Skills & Abilities: Communication: The faculty member must be able to utilize effective communication with peers, students, clients and their families, and other healthcare providers. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to read at a competency level that allows one to safely carry out the essential functions of an assignment (examples: handwritten documentation, printed policy and procedure manuals, clinical guidelines and instructions, course syllabi). Ability to effectively interpret and process information. Ability to effectively communicate (verbally and in writing) with students, peers, clients/families, healthcare professionals, and others within the community. Ability to access information and to communicate and document effectively via computer. Ability to recognize, interpret, and respond to nonverbal behavior of self and others. Behavior: The faculty member must be capable of exercising good judgment, developing empathetic and therapeutic relationships with students, clients and others, and tolerating close and direct physical contact with a diverse population. They will include people of all ages, races, socioeconomic and ethnic backgrounds, as well as individuals with weight disorders, physicals disfigurement, and medical and mental health problems. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to work with multiple clients/families and colleagues at the same time. Ability to foster and maintain cooperative and collegial relationships with students and peers. Critical Thinking: The faculty member must possess sufficient abilities in the areas of calculation, critical problem solving, reasoning, and judgment to be able to comprehend and process information within a reasonable time frame as determined by the profession. The faculty member must be able to prioritize, organize, and attend to talks and responsibilities efficiently. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to collect, interpret and analyze written, verbal and observed data about students. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks, integrate information and make decisions. Ability to apply knowledge of the principles, indications, and contraindications for nursing interventions. Ability to act safely and ethically in the classroom, simulation/skills lab, and in the community. Other Information & Attributes: This position requires a minimum of 12 hours of academic load per year. Overload can be negotiated. Serves as an effective, collegial member of nursing faculty. Contributes to monitoring and evaluating of students. Supports the work and efforts of colleagues in achieving the programmatic, departmental, and institutional mission and vision. Engages collaboratively in the development and attainment of program and course goals. Seeks innovative, cost-effective solutions to programmatic, departmental, and institutional challenges. Exercises effective time management by developing and maintaining timelines for personal tasks and student learning activities. Prioritizes instructional responsibilities and guides students in managing their academic workload Demonstrates an understanding of substantial higher education issues. Participates actively in appropriate state, regional and national professional organizations, as well as community groups. CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\tÂ©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Nursing Program Faculty.html": {
      "title": "Job Title: Nursing Program Faculty",
      "description": "Nursing Program Faculty | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrarâs Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Nursing Program Faculty Nursing Program Faculty Job Posted: March 6, 2026 Job Title: Nursing Program Faculty General Summary : Assistant Professor teaching an average of 24 load hours per academic year. Nursing Program Faculty who has clinical load responsibilities are accountable to the Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty job description in addition to this one.  The position is a 9-month contract that runs from August to May. Primary Duties & Responsibilities : Plan and deliver learning experiences for nursing students to make maximum use of class time. Teach assigned nursing education load. Evaluate student performances in the classroom. Discuss evaluations with students and return evaluation to student file. (Evaluation of student performance includes evaluation of papers, projects, and journals, and returning these to students in timely fashion.) Attend departmental (voting) and institutional faculty (non-voting) meetings. Serve on departmental committees as assigned. Participate in in clinical nursing education, if part of assigned load, abiding by the Nursing Clinical Faculty job description. Participate in the design and development of new health professions programs and in the revision of current health professions programs based on assessment data. Perform other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Qualifications : MSN preferred RN, MSN-in-Process within one year of graduation mandatory. Current, unencumbered, Missouri nursing license. Approval by the Missouri State Board of Nursing as a faculty member. Physical Requirements: Frequently stand for at least one hour consecutively. Operate classroom audio-visual equipment. Speak loudly and clearly enough to be understood by students. Other Skills & Abilities: Communication: The faculty member must be able to utilize effective communication with peers, students, clients and their families, and other healthcare providers. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to read at a competency level that allows one to safely carry out the essential functions of an assignment (examples: handwritten documentation, printed policy and procedure manuals, clinical guidelines and instructions, course syllabi). Ability to effectively interpret and process information. Ability to effectively communicate (verbally and in writing) with students, peers, clients/families, healthcare professionals, and others within the community. Ability to access information and to communicate and document effectively via computer. Ability to recognize, interpret, and respond to nonverbal behavior of self and others. Behavior: The faculty member must be capable of exercising good judgment, developing empathetic and therapeutic relationships with students, clients and others, and tolerating close and direct physical contact with a diverse population. They will include people of all ages, races, socioeconomic and ethnic backgrounds, as well as individuals with weight disorders, physicals disfigurement, and medical and mental health problems. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to work with multiple clients/families and colleagues at the same time. Ability to foster and maintain cooperative and collegial relationships with students and peers. Critical Thinking: The faculty member must possess sufficient abilities in the areas of calculation, critical problem solving, reasoning, and judgment to be able to comprehend and process information within a reasonable time frame as determined by the profession. The faculty member must be able to prioritize, organize, and attend to talks and responsibilities efficiently. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to collect, interpret and analyze written, verbal and observed data about students. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks, integrate information and make decisions. Ability to apply knowledge of the principles, indications, and contraindications for nursing interventions. Ability to act safely and ethically in the classroom, simulation/skills lab, and in the community. Other Information and Attributes: This is a 09-month position and has a required minimum of 24 hours of academic load per year. Overload can be negotiated. Serves as an effective, collegial member of nursing faculty. Contributes to monitoring and evaluating of students. Supports the work and efforts of colleagues in achieving the programmatic, departmental, and institutional mission and vision. Contributes creatively and helpfully to setting and meeting goals. Seeks innovative, cost-effective solutions to programmatic, departmental, and institutional challenges. Sets and meets timelines; prioritizes own work and that of students. Demonstrates an understanding of substantial higher education issues. Participates actively in appropriate state, regional and national professional organizations, as well as community groups. Application Process: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\tÂ©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/job-listing1.html": {
      "title": "Job Title: Graduate Assistant-Strength & Conditioning",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant-Strength and Conditioning | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrarâs Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Graduate Assistant-Strength and Conditioning Graduate Assistant-Strength and Conditioning Date Posted: December 8, 2025 Job Title: Graduate Assistant-Strength & Conditioning General Summary : Responsibilities include working with all phases of the strength and conditioning program that include but are not limited to: working with various athletic programs to develop physical strength, flexibility, speed, and agility utilizing program(s) designed to each athletic program’s needs.  Coordinating with athletic staff on scheduling and the status of the program and /or student-athletes.  Promoting a positive atmosphere in the facility.  Assisting with the general upkeep of equipment and the facility. Other duties as assigned. Develop a familiarity with NAIA rules and maintain the integrity of the athletic program through the appropriate application of these rules. Provide excellent customer service to our students, donors, sponsors, alumni and all of our internal and external constituents. Primary Duties & Responsibilities : 70% - Work with various athletic programs on strength and conditioning 20% - Coordinate with athletic staff 10% - Other duties as assigned Education & Experience Qualifications : Bachelor's Degree required.  Bachelor’s degree in exercise science or related field preferred. First Aid/ CPR/AED certification. Progress towards CSCS and/or SCCC certification (preference to those already certified). Previous experience in college athletics preferred. Must be accepted in to the graduate program at Central Methodist University. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift 50lbs, stand on your feet for periods of three to five hours.  Bending, walking, kneeling, stretching, and stooping. Set up equipment and facility as needed Other Skills & Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively in both written and verbal form.  Experience with Microsoft Word. Other Information & Attributes: . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\tÂ©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Academic Support Specialist CLAS.html": {
      "title": "Academic Support Specialist (CLAS)",
      "description": "Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) Date Posted: August 13, 2026 Job Title: Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) GENERAL SUMMARY : To provide academic support to CMU’s Fayette Campus Students.  This includes but not limited to registration, transfer work and withdraws and day to day functions of the Registrar’s Office pertaining to CLAS (College of Liberal Arts & Sciences) students. This is a full-time position with benefits. This position is located on the Fayette Campus. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Process all CMU transcript requests-35% Assist with and enter the transfer work of CLAS students-20% Assist and Process all CLAS add/drop/withdraws forms-30% Manages CLAS wait lists-5% Process electronic updated information through CARS (Campus Administration & Registration System)-5% Maintains CLAS files, filing included-5% Other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Associates degree preferred, not required. High School Diploma, Required. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to work at a computer for long periods of time, filing and periodic lifting up to 15 lbs.  Must be able to stand and speak to students at a counter. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented. Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Admissions Specialist for College of Graduate and Extended Studies.html": {
      "title": "Admissions Specialist",
      "description": "Admissions Specialist - College of Graduate & Extended Studies | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Admissions Specialist - College of Graduate & Extended Studies Admissions Specialist - College of Graduate & Extended Studies Date Posted: September 4, 2026 Job Title: Admissions Specialist - College of Graduate & Extended Studies GENERAL SUMMARY:  This position is responsible for maintaining the student database by entering, verifying, and correcting application and new student data, processing transcripts, organization of committee appeals, management of incoming digital forms, oversight of CGES (College of Graduate & Extended Studies) Admissions general inbox, and contacting prospective students with reminders and updates.  Other duties, as assigned. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Accurately process incoming test scores and transcripts for undergraduate and graduate students 35% Accurately update/modify data in student record system 15% Accurately process undergraduate and graduate applications 10% Accurately view and index images (virtual imaging system) 10% Accurately processes PEP incoming documents 15% Contact prospective students with reminders and updates 10% Accomplish department and organization mission by completing related tasks as needed 5% Perform other duties as assigned. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS: HS Diploma or GED.  2 years of work experience in an office setting that requires accurate data-entry is preferred. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Candidates should be able to work a standard 40-hour week on campus.  Must able to sit or stand for long periods of time in front of a computer. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES:  Candidate must possess the following:  A strong and proven work ethic, be a quick learner, excellent written and verbal communication skills, exceptional attention to detail with proven history of little to no errors in data entry, must be willing to provide excellent customer service at all times.  Experience with data entry, Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Access), email, scanners, and mail merge a must.  Lift 25 lbs., when necessary, stand and/or sit to complete job duties. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: The above is intended to describe the general content of and requirements for the performance of this position.  It is not to be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements. CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Admissions Support Specialist.html": {
      "title": "Admissions Support Specialist",
      "description": "Admissions Support Specialist | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Admissions Support Specialist Admissions Support Specialist Date Posted: July 30, 2026 Job Title: Admissions Support Specialist GENERAL SUMMARY : This position is responsible for maintaining the student database by entering, verifying, and correcting Prison Education Program (PEP) application and new student data, and managing PEP third-party transcript request services. This position is located on the Fayette Campus. PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Accurately process PEP applications and create student files. 30% Accurately manage PEP third party transcript request services. 30% Accurately view and index images (virtual imaging system). 10% Accurately update/modify data in student record system. 10% Contact appropriate staff with reminders and updates. 10% Accomplish department and organization mission by completing related tasks as needed. 10% Other duties, as assigned. MANAGERIAL/SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : Provides work direction for: The College of Graduate and Extended Studies Admissions Office. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : HS Diploma or GED. Associate’s degree in business preferred. Will consider 2+ years of work experience in an office setting that requires accurate data-entry. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Candidates should be able to work a standard 40-hour week on campus. Must be able to sit or stand for long periods of time in front of a computer. Lift 25 lbs., when necessary. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Candidate must possess the following: A strong and proven work ethic, be a quick learner, excellent written and verbal communication skills, exceptional attention to detail with proven history of little to no errors in data entry, must be willing to provide excellent customer service at all times. Experience with data entry, Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook), email, scanners, and mail merge a must. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: The above is intended to describe the general content of and requirements for the performance of this position. It is not to be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements. CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Apprenticeship Coordinator.html": {
      "title": "Apprenticeship Coordinator",
      "description": "Apprenticeship Coordinator | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Apprenticeship Coordinator Apprenticeship Coordinator Date Posted: August 12, 2026 Job Title: Apprenticeship Coordinator GENERAL SUMMARY : The Apprenticeship Coordinator is responsible for the day-to-day administration of the C3 Program, with particular emphasis on maintaining required Department of Labor registered apprenticeship documentation, recruiting and onboarding new participants, managing apprentice records, marketing the program, and maintaining communication with participating school districts and other employer partners. This position is located in Park Hills, MO. The coordinator works collaboratively with university departments, apprenticeship staff, school district representatives, mentors, and state and federal apprenticeship partners to ensure participant records are accurate, program requirements are completed, and CMU remains in compliance with its responsibilities as a registered apprenticeship sponsor. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Process apprenticeship registrations, modifications, transfers, suspensions, cancellations, and completions. Monitor apprentices’ on-the-job learning hours, competency attainment, coursework, mentor evaluations, employment status, and other program requirements. Maintain complete, accurate, confidential, and audit-ready participant records across Department of Labor, institutional, and internal tracking systems. Support file reviews, monitoring visits, audits, and other activities necessary to maintain compliance with institutional, grant, and Department of Labor requirements. Recruit prospective participants through employer and community-college referrals, direct outreach, informational sessions, community events, digital communication, and other marketing efforts. Explain program eligibility, benefits, experiential-credit opportunities, employment expectations, mentorship requirements, and participant responsibilities to prospective apprentices. Respond to prospective-student inquiries, review initial eligibility, and maintain communication from initial interest through onboarding. Guide eligible participants through the apprenticeship application and onboarding process, including the submission of required employment and program documentation. Develop and distribute accurate recruitment materials in collaboration with Admissions, Marketing, and other university departments. Represent the C3 Program at recruitment events, employer meetings, conferences, and community-college events. Guide employers through partnership requirements, mentor selection, evaluations, wage progression, on-the-job learning, and required documentation. Identify apprentices who may be eligible for experiential credit and coordinate the collection, review, and tracking of required course, mentor, and evaluator documentation. Train and support CMU employees involved in recruiting, onboarding, tracking, or assisting apprentices. Develop and maintain procedures, templates, guides, presentations, and other resources supporting consistent program operations. Collaborate with university departments, consortium institutions, Department of Labor representatives, and Missouri apprenticeship partners. Participate in relevant meetings and training and travel to CMU locations, partner organizations, recruitment events, and program meetings as required. Perform other duties as assigned. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor’s Degree required; graduate degree preferred. Candidate should possess superior organization; communication and technology related skills. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Periods of standing, routinely lifting more than 25 pounds, and frequent travel between CMU sites and partners is required/expected in this role. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: This position requires occasional evening work, travel, and use of personal vehicle. MS Office Applications including MS Outlook and Excel; student management systems, learning management systems, electronic calendar; maintain confidentiality of student records. Candidate should be able to operate office equipment including printers, scanners, copiers, and faxes. CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Application Process: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Director of Assessment and Academic Institutional Research Support.html": {
      "title": "Director of Assessment and Academic Institutional Research Support",
      "description": "Director of Assessment and Academic Institutional Research Support | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Director of Assessment and Academic Institutional Research Support Director of Assessment and Academic Institutional Research Support Date Posted: June 3, 2026 Job Title: Director of Assessment and Academic Institutional Research Support General Summary : Provide university-wide leadership and day-to-day coordination of assessment of student learning and program effectiveness across academic units. Provide support for the program review cycle and program-viability assessments. Build capacity through training, manage assessment systems and dashboards, and deliver evidence-based recommendations to academic leadership. _____________________________________________________________________________ Primary Duties & Responsibilities : Core responsibilities Assessment & Learning Outcomes (primary) Lead and coordinate the continuous assessment cycle for undergraduate, graduate, and other programs: outcome writing, curriculum mapping, assessment design, direct/indirect measures, data collection, analysis, and closing the loop. Maintain centralized assessment calendar, repository, and standardized report templates. Provide consultation to faculty and staff on assessment methodology, rubric design, reliable scoring, and interpreting results. Oversee assessment tool(s) administration (e.g., Watermark), ensure data integrity, and manage training. Produce periodic assessment summaries and trend analyses for academic leadership. Program Review & Program Viability (distinct, cyclical) Assist with program review: enrollment trends, retention and completion metrics, student-learning evidence, course and faculty productivity, cost-per-credit and cost-per-graduate, adjunct reliance, and labor-market alignment. Accreditation Maintain an understanding of the requirements of HLC criteria and USDOE policy changes and their institutional implications, as applicable. Conduct periodic compliance audits of assessment and program review activities and remediate gaps. Training, Capacity Building & Communication Design and deliver workshops and one‑on‑one coaching for faculty, staff, and administrators on assessment practices, data literacy, and use of assessment platforms. Serve as institutional consultant for syllabus-level outcomes alignment and capstone assessment design. Communicate results, timelines, and expectations clearly across units; produce concise executive summaries for leadership. Data, Reporting & Decision Support Track action-plan implementation and report closure rates. Aid in determining cohort classifications for incoming students to support institutional data analysis and reporting. Assist with gathering and compiling institutional data for departmental reviews and other reporting needs. Perform other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Qualifications : Requirements for this position include a Master’s degree in a related field and a minimum of 5 years’ experience in higher education administration, with demonstrated significant administrative and teaching responsibilities. Terminal Degree is preferred. Other Skills & Abilities: Must have the ability to operate a personal computer and keyboard, printers, telephone, facsimile, typewriter, and other office equipment. Manual dexterity to handle books, software, and a variety of media formats is necessary. Knowledge of and practice with emerging technologies is preferred.  Strong communication skills and ability to build consensus. Other Information & Attributes: The position will, on occasion, require scheduled evenings and travel to state meetings. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Director of Financial Assistance.html": {
      "title": "Director of Financial Assistance",
      "description": "Director of Financial Assistance | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Director of Financial Assistance Director of Financial Assistance Date Posted: July 17, 2026 Job Title: Director of Financial Assistance GENERAL SUMMARY : Member of the Enrollment Management leadership team responsible for the effective administration of all financial aid programs and policies for CMU students. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Direct and manage student financial aid operations and programs Maintain institutional compliance for Title IV programs Assure proper counsel and advice to students and their families about financial aid opportunities Oversee the maintenance and integrity of information on the financial aid web page Ensure CMU programs and operations are administered in compliance with federal, state and institutional guidelines Hire, train, and supervise student financial assistance staff Keep abreast of financial aid trends, technologies and best practices Work collaboratively with appropriate University personnel to review financial processes and improvements to gain efficiencies and maximize service to students Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Master’s degree-Preferred Bachelor’s Degree-Required; Accounting degree preferred Supervisor experience - Preferred 3-5 years of financial aid or higher education administrative experience - Preferred Excellent communication and organizational skills Knowledge of Prison Education Programs - Preferred OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: General knowledge of accounting principles and methods, data processing systems and computer software. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Typical office setting.   Occasional weekend or evenings for special student events. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
