      "description": "Administrative Assistant-Financial Services | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Administrative Assistant-Financial Services Administrative Assistant-Financial Services Date Posted: September 4, 2026 Job Title: Administrative Assistant-Financial Services General Summary :  The Administrative Assistant is responsible for setting the stage for excellent customer service for the student and/or parent and general correspondence and supply management of the Office of Financial Assistance.  Included in the duties are customer greeting (first point of personal contact for students and parents), answering emails to the general inbox for the office, managing incoming calls and faxes, office supply management, paper and electronic filing. Primary Duties and Responsibilities : 35% Answering general financial aid questions via phone and email or properly distributing phone or email questions to other financial aid personnel for response. 15% Filing of student documents, creating files 15% Greeting incoming students and parents 05% Receiving and managing faxes 10% Electronically filing and indexing financial assistance documents 10% Reports, student record management 05% Daily mail pick up & distribution.  Mailings to students 05% Managing Office Supplies Perform other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Qualifications : High school diploma or equivalent required. Some college preferred. Candidate should have excellent customer service, organizational, communication, and computer skills.  Excellent Microsoft Word, Excel, and Publisher required. Physical Requirements: Occasional lifting of 25 pounds or more; occasional across campus walking; long periods of sitting.  Must be able to speak in a clear manner. Other Skills & Abilities: Candidate should be able to operate office equipment including faxes, printers, and copiers.  Candidate should have professional demeanor and appearance, self-initiative, and be willing to work as a team player. Other Information & Attributes: Position may require occasional evening or weekend work. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
