    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications .html": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant-Athletic Communications",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications  | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications Date Posted: May 19, 2026 Job Title: Graduate Assistant-Athletic Communications General Summary: Assist in the promotion of CMU Athletics (varsity and reserve) through the daily updating of the athletics website; writing and distributing athletics press releases, including game recaps; maintaining official CMU Athletics Facebook, Twitter and Instagram accounts; and managing home (varsity/reserve) contests, including official statistics, announcements, photos, and game programs. Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Assist in updating and maintaining of the CMU athletics website (schedules/results, rosters, photo galleries, etc.); writing, distributing, and posting athletics press releases to website; designing and printing athletics publications (game programs, gameday graphics etc.); set up and production of livestream of varsity contests, maintaining and reporting official statistics; maintain and update social media platforms including Instagram, Twitter (X), and Facebook, creation and editing of video content for the athletic department, coordinating athletics photos, photography and other assigned duties. Perform other duties as assigned. Managerial/Supervisory Responsibilities: Assist in the supervision of student workers in both office and game-day settings. Education & Experience Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree in journalism, communications, sports management, or related field. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to balance multiple tasks and projects to complete them efficiently and on time. Knowledge and/or background in athletics, including statistical record keeping a plus. Excellent computer skills desirable. Physical Requirements: Some lifting up to 40 lbs. necessary. Other Skills & Abilities: Proficient in Adobe InDesign, Adobe Photoshop, Adobe Premier Pro, Microsoft Word and Microsoft Excel. Experience with Presto Stats and web page design preferred. Understanding of and open-mindedness to new technologies. Other Information & Attributes: Regularly requires evening and weekend work. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Graduate Assistant Athletics Creative Content.html": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant-Athletics/Creative Content",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant-Athletics-Creative Content | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Graduate Assistant-Athletics-Creative Content Graduate Assistant-Athletics-Creative Content Date Posted: May 20, 2026 Job Title: Graduate Assistant-Athletics/Creative Content General Summary: Support the communications efforts for the athletics department and its 22 varsity sports and eight reserve sports by contributing high-quality photos and video content, coordinating social media efforts, and producing marketing content to enhance the game day experience. Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Shooting, producing, and editing video content for various platforms; Assisting with the photography and videography of media days; Brainstorm, create, and publish both graphic and video content across the athletic department’s social media channels (Twitter, Facebook, Instagram), website, YouTube, and other platforms; Contribute to the maintenance, organization, and oversight of the overall content calendar; Perform other duties as assigned. Managerial/Supervisory Responsibilities: Assist in the supervision of student workers in both office and game-day settings. Education & Experience Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree within the preferred area of study of Digital Media, Film, and Broadcasting, Communications, Journalism, Public Relations, or Sports Management. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to balance multiple tasks and projects in order to complete them efficiently and on time. Knowledge and/or background in athletics, Excellent computer skills desirable. Physical Requirements: Some lifting up to 40 lbs. necessary. Other Skills & Abilities: Proficient or basic knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite programs (Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro, After Effects); Experience in advanced content creation, including video and photo shooting and editing skills; An understanding of relevant social media platforms Other Information & Attributes: Regularly requires evening and weekend work. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Campus Safety Officer.html": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Campus Safety Officer | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Campus Safety Officer Campus Safety Officer Date Posted: August 18, 2026 Job Title: Campus Safety Officer G GENERAL SUMMARY : Professional safety officer to provide excellent customer service to our students, faculty and staff.   Provide protection to assets, personnel, and students and to report any suspicious behavior on and around campus to authorities.  This person will maintain a highly visible presence and promote a safe, secure and responsible campus atmosphere.Detecting, deterring, observing and reporting are key duties. This is a full-time position. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Protect University employees, students and property by promoting a safe campus and safety awareness. Observe campus and facilities for signs of crime, vandalism and unsafe behavior and investigate as needed. Initiate proactive means of protecting life or property. Take accurate notes and make reports of unusual or suspicious occurrences. Regularly patrol campus and facilities. Monitor and control access at building entrances. Monitor parking lots and enforce parking regulations. Monitor alarm systems and video cameras and operate emergency systems. Perform basic First Aid, CPR and AED. Assist Grounds and Maintenance with snow removal Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : High School diploma or GED. Work experience as a security/safety guard or in a related field. Customer Service Experience. Ability to operate vehicles and equipment and valid driver’s license. Excellent knowledge of public safety and security procedures/protocols. Surveillance skills and attention to detail. ALICE training (Can be provided on site). PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to lift 75lbs. Must be able to spend extended periods on foot whether standing or walking in varying weather conditions. Must be able to work in extreme weather conditions. Must be able to climb stairs, and ladders. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Computer knowledge to send and receive email messages. Word processing (Daily Safety Activity Reports). Microsoft Excel (data entry) Understanding of Campus Alert System and how it works. Basic understanding of smart phone systems and usage. Integrity and professionalism OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: The standard schedule for this position is 12:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m. on Saturdays and Sundays and 4:00 p.m. – 12:00 a.m. on Monday & Tuesdays. Schedule is subject to change based on operational needs, including staffing levels, call-ins, approved time off, or adjustments made by the supervisor. Work Schedules will include working on holidays and as needed for special events. Pre-employment Background Screening required. This is an essential personnel position and is required to be on campus during designated work hours. Essential security positions are required to be at work even if campus is closed due to inclement weather. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t© 2026"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time.html": {
      "title": "Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time",
      "description": "Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time Job Title:  Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-time Date Posted:  2/16/2026 Reports To: Provost FLSA Classification:  Non-Exempt GENERAL SUMMARY : This is a part-time position that works within the state of Missouri Correctional Facilities to provide support for prison education program students. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Hold study hall for a set period of time, dependent on correctional facility Check high school equivalency information in AS 400 Regularly review conduct violations of students for continued participation in AS400 Manage the call out list for study hall each week Manage the Lantern class for communication for the correctional facility Assist students with questions Assist with registration and financial aid activities, as needed Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor’s degree preferred.  Correctional facility experience is preferred. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Frequently stand and/or sit for several hours consecutively. May work in buildings without elevator access, requiring routine use of stairways to move between floors. May work in areas of a facility without air conditioning. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Microsoft Office experience preferred, Canvas LMS experience preferred, AS400 experience preferred OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: This position may require travel, evenings, use of a personal vehicle, and required to enter a correctional facility. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. APPLY TODAY CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Housekeeping 2nd Shift.html": {
      "title": "Position Title: Housekeeping- 2ndShift (1:00 pm-9:30 pm)",
      "description": "Housekeeping- 2nd Shift | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Housekeeping 2nd Shift Housekeeping- 2nd Shift Position Title: Housekeeping- 2 nd Shift (1:00 pm-9:30 pm) GENERAL SUMMARY: Perform a regular cleaning schedule for campus facilities. Report any maintenance problems. Maintain public restrooms, shower rooms and building and hall common area.  This position is full time position and is benefit eligible.  The opening is for 2 nd shift, Mon – Fri 1:00pm – 9:30pm - Shift hours are flexible. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Ensure the assigned departmental building areas are cleaned on a scheduled basis. Remove trash to designated pickup points. Report building system problems to Facilities office. Adequately stock restrooms with paper products and soap. Disinfect designated areas as required. Strip and recoat designated floors. Clean carpets and floor tile. Perform full housekeeping duties during assigned work hours. Other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : One year in Custodial Services preferred. High School diploma preferred. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to lift 50 lbs. Full range of physical motion. Operate a variety of cleaning equipment. Work in some heat extremes during summer. Must be able to navigate up and down stairs OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Must be able to work with other housekeeping staff as a team, as well as cover other buildings when short staffed. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Occasional overtime and weekend work for special events. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.  They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.   Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Dean of School of Health Professionals.html": {
      "title": "Dean of School of Health Professionals",
      "description": "Dean of School of Health Professionals | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Dean of School of Health Professionals Dean of School of Health Professionals Date Posted: September 21, 2026 Job Title: Dean of the School of Health Professions GENERAL SUMMARY : This is a 12-month administrative position with faculty rank. Responsible for the development, accreditation, and oversight of Health Professions programming in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) and the College of Graduate and Extended Studies (CGES). PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : 30% Monitor the function of the School of Health Professions programs and faculty to maintain program effectiveness, accreditation standard compliance, and budgetary parameters; 30% Act in conjunction with the Program Director for each program of study to assure the cohesion, caliber, and accreditation of the education programs. 15% Market programs to the healthcare community, inclusive of prospective students and faculty. 25% Work closely with the Associate Provost for Innovation to enhance all aspects of the provision of education, the financial accountability of programming, the well-being of all faculty, staff, and students, and the general good reputation enjoyed by CMU. Perform other duties as assigned. MANAGERIAL/SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : At least 75-100% of time is spent in managerial capacity. Directly supervises Program Directors, the Clinical Coordinators, and staff. Overload may be negotiated. Evaluate Program Directors, faculty, and staff performance annually and as needed. Discuss evaluations with faculty and provide copy to the Provost’s office, and the employee file. Guide faculty development. Resource day-to-day programmatic management by the Program Directors. Oversee the resolution of programmatic issues and complaints. Attend programmatic, departmental, and institutional faculty meetings. Participate in the recruitment and retention of students; Approve contractual agreements with clinical agencies prior to their submission to Senior Staff for signature. Liaison with the Assistant Dean of Online Programming to assure course structure and schedule parameters are communicated to Program Directors and remain in congruence with CMU guidelines and requirements; Ensure the Program Coordinators for the BSN-G, BSN-C, and ABSN maintain the congruency of coursework and evaluation strategies for the bachelor’s-level programs; Ensure appropriate faculty recruitment; Provide leadership to the faculty in curriculum development, implementation and evaluation; Serve on University-wide, CLAS, or CGES committees as requested; Oversee the accreditation processes for all programs and ensure appropriate compliance with standards; Meet regularly with Program Directors. Preside at Divisional meetings. Oversee the development of programmatic budgets and submit them to the Provost of the University. Oversee budget expenditures. Provide leadership in total program assessment/revision and new program development. Assist with development and implementation of new graduate programs. Further professional development by participation in professional organizations and/or continuing education programs and workshops. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Administrative experience preferred. PhD in nursing or related field (with MSN) or DNP required Current, unencumbered, Missouri nursing license. Approval by the Missouri State Board of Nursing as a faculty member. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Frequently stand and/or sit for at least one hour consecutively. Operate classroom and meeting audio-visual equipment. Speak loudly and clearly enough to be understood by students. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Communication: The Program Administrator must be able to utilize effective communication with peers, subordinates, students and their families, other educational providers, and other constituents of the community of interest. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to effectively interpret and process written and verbal information. Ability to effectively communicate (verbally and in writing). Ability to access information and to communicate and document effectively via computer. Ability to recognize, interpret, and respond to nonverbal behavior of self and others. Consistently demonstrate a professional presentation that upholds the Central Methodist University mission statements and philosophy. Behavior: The Program Administrator must be capable of exercising good judgment, developing empathetic and therapeutic relationships with others. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to work with multiple students/families and colleagues at the same time. Ability to foster and maintain cooperative and collegial relationships with students, faculty, and peers. Ability to provide faculty leadership and support faculty development. Critical Thinking: The Program Administrator must possess sufficient abilities in the areas of calculation, critical problem solving, reasoning, and judgment to be able to comprehend and process information within a reasonable time frame. The Program Administrator must be able to prioritize, organize, and attend to responsibilities efficiently. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to collect, interpret and analyze written, verbal and observed data. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks, integrate information and make decisions. Ability to apply knowledge of the principles, indications, and contraindications for nursing educational processes. Ability to act safely and ethically in the classroom and in the community. Ability to lead others in a professional manner. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Serves as an effective, collegial member of the faculty. Supports the work and efforts of colleagues in achieving the programmatic, departmental, and institutional mission and vision. Contributes creatively and helpfully to setting and meeting goals. Seeks innovative, cost-effective solutions to programmatic, departmental, and institutional challenges. Sets and meets timelines; prioritizes own work and that of faculty. Demonstrates an understanding of substantial higher education issues. Participates actively in appropriate state, regional and national professional organizations, as well as community groups. CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t© 2026"
    },
    "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Instructor Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano.html": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano",
      "description": "Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar’s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano Date Posted: September 18, 2026 Job Title: Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano GENERAL SUMMARY : The Swinney Conservatory of Music at Central Methodist University invites applications for a full-time non-tenure track Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano to begin Fall 2027 (title will be determined by achieved degree of selected candidate). The successful candidate will be an excellent pianist and musician who enjoys collaborating with students and faculty. PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : 75%: Play piano on campus for studio lessons, recital rehearsals and performances, choral rehearsals and performances, and opera productions 10%: Travel with students and faculty to regional festivals/competitions for performances and with the Chorale on their annual Fall Choir Tour 15%: Teach keyboard techniques courses, applied piano lessons, and accompanying skills as necessary; organize weekly student recital programs Be adept at playing various genres and styles of music Excellent sight-reading skills Efficient rehearsal technique Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : A master’s or terminal degree in music is preferred, but a bachelor’s prepared candidate with sufficient skill and experience will be considered. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: The collaborative pianist must be able to rehearse for extended periods of time.  Negotiating stairs and walking quickly between studios may be required. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Strong time management skills Strong communication skills Enthusiasm for working with college students at a variety of skill levels OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: This position will require some work in evenings, on weekends, and/or travel. CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive, and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.  Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.  CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t©"
    }
